# GitHub reads this file to offer "Cite this repository" (APA and BibTeX).
#
# There is deliberately no `version` or `date-released`: CI tags every green build
# of main, so any version written here would be stale by the next push. A citation
# without one points at the repository, which is the stable thing to cite.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: diskqueue
abstract: >-
  A generic, durable, FIFO disk-backed queue for Go: a persistent work queue that
  doubles as a write-ahead log. Records are fsync'd before Add returns, every
  record and segment header carries an xxhash64 checksum, damage is dropped and
  counted rather than delivered, and reopening reads one 64-byte header per
  segment instead of the backlog.
authors:
  - family-names: Lindvall
    given-names: Johan
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohanLindvall/diskqueue"
url: "https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/JohanLindvall/diskqueue"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - go
  - golang
  - persistent queue
  - disk-backed queue
  - write-ahead log
  - durability
  - fsync
  - crash recovery
  - data integrity
